# Snyk (https://snyk.io) policy file, patches or ignores known vulnerabilities.
version: v1.25.1
# ignores vulnerabilities until expiry date; change duration by modifying expiry date
ignore:
  SNYK-JS-REACTROUTER-18313144:
    - 'react-router-dom > react-router':
        reason: >-
          Open Redirect (backslash paths), fixed only in react-router 7.18.0;
          the move to v7 is ENG-437. Not reachable in the portal: it routes
          with <HashRouter> (declarative, no data router, loaders, actions or
          redirect()), so every href and navigate() target is the current
          document URL plus '#' plus the path (createHashHref), and a
          backslash path stays in the fragment on the same origin. The portal
          also never builds a navigation target from URL or user input:
          targets are literals, server-issued submission ids and form slugs,
          the canonical /kapps/... redirect, or a backPath held in history
          state that only the portal sets (from location.pathname or
          constants). Checked for ENG-436 against react-router-dom 6.30.6.
        expires: 2027-02-15T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-11-17T19:22:23.000Z
  SNYK-JS-REACTROUTER-18313130:
    - 'react-router-dom > react-router':
        reason: >-
          Unsafe Reflection in deserializeErrors during SSR hydration, fixed
          only in react-router 7.18.0; the move to v7 is ENG-437. Not
          reachable: the advisory applies only to Framework or Data Mode with
          SSR/hydration, and the portal is a client-only Vite SPA using
          <HashRouter> (no createBrowserRouter/RouterProvider, no hydrateRoot,
          no hydration data).
        expires: 2027-02-15T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-11-17T19:22:23.000Z
  SNYK-JS-DOMPURIFY-21460657:
    - '@toast-ui/react-editor > @toast-ui/editor > dompurify':
        reason: >-
          @toast-ui/editor 3.2.2 (its last line; 3.2.3 still requires
          dompurify ^2.3.3) inlines its own copy of DOMPurify 2.3.3 in
          dist/esm/index.js, so no resolution or upgrade can reach it, and
          there is no fixed 2.x release. The portal uses the editor only in
          the Kinetic form Markdown widget: the Editor for user-written
          WYSIWYG markdown and HTML, and the Viewer (and the Editor's initial
          value) for the markdown stored in the field. DOMPurify sanitizes the
          HTML in that markdown, including HTML embedded in it. The stored
          value can come from any writer of the field: another user, an
          anonymous submitter where the form allows anonymous access, or the
          API or workflow. The copy that ships is DOMPurify 2.3.3, older than
          the 2.5.9 Snyk evaluates, so these IDs are a lower bound: advisories
          fixed between 2.3.4 and 2.5.9 apply too. This is real exposure,
          accepted for 7.0.0 by Matt (2026-11-17). Replacing the editor is
          ENG-438, which removes these ignores.
        expires: 2027-02-15T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-11-17T19:22:23.000Z
