          the 2.5.9 Snyk evaluates, so these IDs are a lower bound: advisories
          fixed between 2.3.4 and 2.5.9 apply too. This is real exposure,
          accepted for 7.0.0 by Matt (2026-11-17). Replacing the editor is
          ENG-438, which removes these ignores.
        expires: 2027-02-15T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-11-17T19:22:23.000Z
  SNYK-JS-DOMPURIFY-18170233:
    - '@toast-ui/react-editor > @toast-ui/editor > dompurify':
        reason: >-
          @toast-ui/editor 3.2.2 (its last line; 3.2.3 still requires
          dompurify ^2.3.3) inlines its own copy of DOMPurify 2.3.3 in
          dist/esm/index.js, so no resolution or upgrade can reach it, and
          there is no fixed 2.x release. The portal uses the editor only in
          the Kinetic form Markdown widget: the Editor for user-written
          WYSIWYG markdown and HTML, and the Viewer (and the Editor's initial
          value) for the markdown stored in the field. DOMPurify sanitizes the
          HTML in that markdown, including HTML embedded in it. The stored
          value can come from any writer of the field: another user, an
          anonymous submitter where the form allows anonymous access, or the
          API or workflow. The copy that ships is DOMPurify 2.3.3, older than
          the 2.5.9 Snyk evaluates, so these IDs are a lower bound: advisories
